data/
mirror/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The publisher key, written next to the script that generates it. This
# repository is public: committing this file would hand the key to everyone
# and make the sealing worthless.
YOUR-SECRET-KEY.txt
MIRROR-ADDRESS.txt

# The licensing keys. The private one mints licences this application will
# accept, and the content keys decrypt every published bundle — this
# repository is public, so committing either would hand away the whole thing
# in a way no later commit could take back.
PUBLISHER-PRIVATE.key
PUBLISHER-PUBLIC.txt
CONTENT-KEYS.json
*.btlicence
m.bin
